Ability to poly, at least as a one-shot, isn't hard to come by. You'll
probably see at least a polytrap or a chameleon corpse during the
early game. (Suriving the early game is, itself, very rough under the
circumstances.)

Poly control is indeed a WAGPTTRNG. The best idea I've come up with is
to get randomly polyed into a metallivore, then gobble rings. I've
actually managed the first part (rock mole), but changed back before I
could get to where the rings are. (Having an ID'ed ring in your
starting inventory is a bonus, but the classes that start with rings
tend to not be the most survivable sans inventory.)

Price ID (via stand and #chat) is another possibility; the only really
nasty ring to eat would be hunger ($100) while poly control is
$300. Those that modify stats last only as long as your current form.
And actually, I can easily imagine reaching a state where intrinsic
hunger could be an advantage.

That's all in the context of hoping that the RNG is a kind and
merciful RNG, and not a wrathful RNG that makes the important ring
types be made of inedible materials.

OTOH, the list of monsters that have levitation, water-walking,
magical breathing, flying, swimming, wall-walking, amphibiousness
and/or breathlessness isn't short. It doesn't take that much luck for
a random poly to give you something that can traverse the static
hazards of the castle level one way or another. (Getting _to_ the
castle in that form, and surviving the occupants, are other matters.)

Being a Xorn with intrinsic unchanging might make things a _lot_
easier all around. While we're at it, I want a pony, a million
dollars, a nice comfy chair and a good solid C compiler.

